From: Codex <codex@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] user32, comctl32: create the XP shell's controls from Wine's themed controls

Purpose: draw buttons, edits, list boxes and combo boxes in the XP shell's
windows and dialogs with the theme.
XP behavior: the XP shell's dialogs (Run, Folder Options, property sheets)
and the folder window's address bar use themed v6 controls. The address
bar's drop-down button fills the client height inside the one-pixel frame,
and CB_GETITEMHEIGHT(-1) returns the height set with CB_SETITEMHEIGHT
(Wine's tests mark this todo_wine), from which ComboBoxEx sizes the band to
22 pixels.
Wine before: the XP shell runs the native comctl32 without its SxS
activation context, so it got user32's classic Button, ComboBox, Edit,
ListBox and Static.
Change: in a process of the external shell whose comctl32 is native,
user32 creates those classes from Wine's themed implementations in
win4wine-controls.dll, registered as "win4wine!" + name with the prefix as
their version, so that GetClassName still reports Button, Edit and so on.
The alias's ComboBox follows the XP measurements above.
Evidence: tests/toolbar-layout.c reports XP's folder window layout, and the
drop-down button's pixels equal XP's.
Scope: only with WIN4WINE_EXTERNAL_SHELL and a native comctl32; processes
with Wine's own comctl32 are not affected.
Old patches: 0060, 0068.
